cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Reasoning allocation: overhead-aware subtree scheduling in SCIP"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-14"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/reasoning-allocation"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/reasoning-allocation"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Research software for allocating bounded SCIP subtree leases using local
  predictions of optimization progress and execution cost. The completed
  cold-request study used 60 independent generated weighted-set-cover templates,
  one fitted model bundle, two timing repeats and three deadlines, producing
  2,520 requests. No registered positive superiority was established; the local
  adaptive bidder lost to a simple estimate-based one-node selector, while other
  directional comparisons remained inconclusive. A pooled-control Monte Carlo
  stability diagnostic failed. The repository preserves scoped findings,
  resource accounting, solver correctness checks and reproducibility records.
  Full raw-result authentication requires external retained research assets.
keywords:
  - metareasoning
  - computation allocation
  - mixed-integer optimization
  - branch and bound
  - SCIP
  - reproducible research
